STEP 1
THINK have Beginning of build; empty workspace.
THINK goal Establishes base anchor beam for front frame section
THINK part beam3-1 (32523 Technic Beam 1 x 3): at center frame origin; fixed
THINK part pin-1 (2780 Technic Pin with Friction Ridges Lengthwise): in beam3-1 hole 1; fixed
THINK part pin-2 (2780 Technic Pin with Friction Ridges Lengthwise): in beam3-1 hole 3; fixed
THINK touches pin-1's pin1 goes into beam3-1's hole1 (stiff)
THINK touches pin-2's pin1 goes into beam3-1's hole3 (stiff)
THINK does beam3-1 holds pin-1
THINK does beam3-1 holds pin-2
THINK why 3-hole beam with friction pins provides rigid two-point mounting
THINK role beam3-1 in the chassis frame: Front cross-member beam
THINK role pin-1 in the chassis frame: Structural connector pin
THINK role pin-2 in the chassis frame: Structural connector pin
THINK check pin-1.pin1 goes into beam3-1.hole1, 0.9 hole deep, held stiff by friction
THINK check pin-2.pin1 goes into beam3-1.hole3, 0.9 hole deep, held stiff by friction
THINK mechanism beam3-1 becomes the structural support of the steering linkage
THINK state steering_linkage has 1 of 1 parts, complete
THINK later Allows perpendicular side beams to attach in step 2 Pattern: two-pin mount
ADD beam3-1 32523 black
ADD pin-1 2780 black
ADD pin-2 2780 black
CONNECT pin-1.pin1 -> beam3-1.hole1 STIFF
CONNECT pin-2.pin1 -> beam3-1.hole3 STIFF
